  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "none",
      "statement": "Three new third-party rows accurately state pinned versions, Cargo SPDX metadata, ring mixed-source license boundary and dev-only rcgen scope."
    },
    {
      "severity": "boundary",
      "statement": "ring is not pure Rust: C/assembly, build-time cc and platform-specific crypto paths remain transitive dependencies. No FIPS claim or arbitrary target compatibility is established."
    },
    {
      "severity": "boundary",
      "statement": "ring default alloc/dev_urandom_fallback features are enabled transitively. Current Rustls/Tokio defaults are disabled; this is not a claim that all transitive defaults are disabled."
    },
    {
      "severity": "boundary",
      "statement": "ring SystemRandom delegates to OS getrandom, and its first fill may synchronously block. Tokio five-second timeout is an asynchronous deadline, not preemption of synchronous crypto/RNG work inside a poll."
    },
    {
      "severity": "boundary",
      "statement": "set_buffer_limit(65536) bounds the two write-direction Rustls buffers separately. It is not a 64KiB total-connection RSS cap, does not cap all peer-certificate/crypto allocations, and does not replace application backpressure/deadlines."
    },
    {
      "severity": "boundary",
      "statement": "Rustls fixed handshake reassembly MAX_HANDSHAKE_SIZE=0xffff is source evidence. No load/fuzz/RSS or timing measurement was executed by this reviewer."
    },
    {
      "severity": "boundary",
      "statement": "Production normal/build metadata graph excludes rcgen/time/yasna/x509-parser. Metadata/lock include all-target and optional edges; recorded host feature tree is narrower and excludes x509-parser. Neither lock presence nor metadata superset alone proves a package was compiled into a production artifact."
    },
